#N canvas 20 20 4500 1800 12;
#X text 20 20 g_grid -- the Launchpad's 108 addressable LEDs \, and their sole owner (C-5). g_oled's arbiter shape: layers with a priority and a time to live \, redrawn by a frame clock. ref/module/display.md, f 58;
#X text 20 170 creation arg 1: the Launchpad's Pd MIDI output port (1 on the device). inlet 0: surface ownership from m_launchpad \, 1 while in Programmer Mode. inlet 1: the beat number within the bar \, from u_root's c_clock. inlet 2: the drum page's state \, from c_steps. inlet 3: the synth choice \, from c_synth. inlet 4: tap \, from u_tempo \, on each tap of page 1's tap pad. outlets: none., f 58;
#X text 20 320 One deviation from g_oled: home is a composite of regions \, the mode lamps down the left column and the beat row along the bottom -- on page 2 the drum page instead of the beat row \, on page 3 the synth pads above it \, on page 1 the tap pad -- while modal and alert take the whole surface., f 58;
#X text 20 520 g_grid owns the LEDs and m_launchpad owns the mode. The first frame after ownership paints all 108 indices \, so that frame is the init clear., f 58;
