#X text 1300 170 C-8: select 2's reject carries the page itself \, so t b b turns it into the beat row's two bangs., f 40;
#X text 2100 1420 Page 2 is the drum page: the beat row gives way \, and each row of the layout table paints one cell. The step cells are four rows of eight \, and c_steps' bar says how many of a row's eight hold steps: a cell is the step its row and column mean \, row r and column c from 0 being step r x row + c + 1 \, and a cell past the row is dark. A step is dim when off \, its velocity's color when on \, white for the softest to red for the loudest \, green under the playhead \, and dark past the selected track's last step. Each velocity button is its own color \, the selected pad red and the other pads bright pink. Every Nth step from step 1 is blue \, N the time signature's top number \, unless it is lit \, and dark past the last step like the rest. The top row of the right 4x4 is the repeat pads \, dim purple \, the one held bright., f 60;
#X obj 2100 1000 t f f f;
#X obj 2180 1100 <= 16;
#X obj 2280 1060 r \$0-dlast;
#X obj 2350 960 t f f;
#X obj 2420 1020 * -8;
#X obj 2350 1060 +;
#X obj 2350 1110 + 135;
#X text 2620 1020 The selected pad is 154 \, red \, and the rest 144 \, bright pink (Brendan \, 2026-11-05): near black they read too indistinct \, and a dim pink with a bright one too faint., f 30;
#X text 2100 1560 A step past the last step is dark \, lit or not: <= gives 1 inside and 0 past it \, which is the off color and gates the on one. A cell past its row gets step 33 \, past every last step \, so it is dark the same way. A color of 128 or more is an RGB entry in paint's table: 128 + level - 1 at full brightness \, 136 + level - 1 at a quarter \, 144 for a pad not selected \, bright pink \, and 154 for the selected pad \, red (Brendan \, 2026-11-05). 145 is a blue step \, every Nth: the off color is inside x (1 + 144 x ((step - 1) mod N == 0)) \, so 1 \, 145 or 0 \, dark. 146 is a repeat pad \, 147 the one held. A step is the level c_steps sends \, 0 for off \, and a velocity button its own level \, full when selected., f 60;
