#X text 3100 900 Page 3's synth pads \, after the beat row: cut-it-synth-page.txt names each cell's synth \, and u_map reads the same file \, so a press and its lamp cannot disagree. Each is its synth's color \, full when chosen and a quarter when not: 146 + 2n + (n is not the choice) \, n 1 for fm and 2 for strings \, so 148 and 149 are fm's entries in paint's RGB table and 150 and 151 strings'. The choice starts at fm \, c_synth's own. unpack sends the synth before the cell \, so the row's n is parked when the cell bangs it., f 50;
