#X text 1300 1700 A step cell's number in the layout table is its place in four rows of eight \, and the expr turns it into the step it shows: row r and column c from 0 are step r x row + c + 1 \, row the steps in a row from c_steps' bar <N> <row> (ref/module/display.md). A cell past the row is 33 \, past every last step \, so dark. Until c_steps says \, row is 0 and every step cell dark., f 40;
