#X obj 1800 640 array set \$0-rgb;
#X text 20 1000 t f b b fires right to left: the type \, then the index \, then the color \, so a spec's bytes cannot swap. An RGB color reads its three bytes red first: t f f f fires right to left too., f 40;
#X text 1800 760 The RGB entries \, three bytes each \, 0 to 127: the drum page's eight velocity levels at full brightness \, white for level 1 falling evenly to red for level 8 \, then the same eight at a quarter \, then a drum pad not selected \, bright pink \, then a bar's first step \, blue \, and a repeat pad \, dim purple and bright purple when held \, then page 3's synth pads \, fm amber and strings cyan \, each full and at a quarter \, then page 1's tap pad \, yellow at a quarter and full while it flashes \, then the selected drum pad \, red. g_grid writes 128 + k to the surface for entry k., f 50;
